Native table constraints inside CaDiCaL 3.0.1 -- the local modifications
=======================================================================

This is the complete diff of `vendor/cadical-3.0.1/src` against the
pristine upstream import (commit d0624a2, byte-identical to the
`mrs-cadical-sys` 0.2.3 copy of CaDiCaL 3.0.1).  It is what `sat -b
cadical --boxes … --boxes-native` relies on; see
`doc/data/boxes_native_propagator_2026-09-26.txt` for the design and the
measurements, and `doc/box_status_2026-09-25.md` (addendum) for the
verdict.

To re-apply after replacing the vendored source with a newer upstream:

    git apply --3way vendor/cadical-3.0.1-native-tables.patch

(it was generated with `git diff d0624a2 HEAD -- vendor/cadical-3.0.1/src`;
`patch -p1 < vendor/cadical-3.0.1-native-tables.patch` works too).

What it changes, all of it inert until `Solver::add_table` is called:

  cadical.hpp, solver.cpp   Solver::add_table (vars, rows): freezes and
                            internalises the variables, hands the rows to
                            Internal::add_table.  Refused with a proof
                            tracer attached.
  internal.hpp              TTable (vars, kill masks per variable and
                            value, the full-rows mask) and the per-variable
                            occurrence lists, reasons, touched list and
                            scratch; the declarations.
  internal.cpp              enlarge (): grow the per-variable table arrays.
  propagate.cpp             add_table (folds the root assignment in), the
                            live rows as a reversible sparse bitset per
                            table: the trail is applied to the tables from
                            an independent pointer (table_sync, at the
                            fixpoint of clause propagation: inprocessors
                            assign root units past the loop's pointer),
                            each literal ANDing its kill mask into the
                            non-zero words (table_assign), saving changed
                            words and the limit once per level on an undo
                            stack; changed tables are then visited: a
                            variable with no live
                            row of one value is forced with the
                            external_reason sentinel (residues make the
                            check one word), a dead table becomes a
                            learned conflict clause built in place, or a
                            root unit, or the empty clause; lazy reasons as
                            trail-order kill covers through the
                            external-clause path; CADICAL_TABLE_STATS=1
                            counters and CADICAL_TABLE_TRACE=1 tracing.
  backtrack.cpp             tables_backtrack: restore the undo stack and
                            lower the applied-trail pointer to the kept
                            literals, which are re-applied.
  solver.cpp                Solver::solve: on SAT, every table is checked
                            against the model (abort on a violation).
  external_propagate.cpp    learn_external_reason_clause: a table-forced
                            literal's reason comes from its table.
  compact.cpp               compaction folds root-fixed variables into
                            the tables, drops fully assigned tables, and
                            renumbers the rest.
  lucky.cpp                 no lucky-phase answers while tables exist.

